net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: unregister netdevice notifier on probe defer

mtk_add_mac() registers a per-MAC netdevice_notifier, but the error path
taken when mtk_mdio_init() returns -EPROBE_DEFER (e.g. a PHY reset GPIO on a
not-yet-probed i2c-mux/expander) is err_free_dev -> mtk_free_dev(), which
only frees the netdevs and never unregisters the notifier. On the deferred
re-probe mtk_add_mac() then warns "notifier callback mtk_device_event already
registered" and the probe spins forever, leaving the ethernet dead.

Unregister the notifier in mtk_free_dev() too (mirroring mtk_unreg_dev). The
err_unreg_netdev path may unregister it first; the second call is a harmless
no-op (unregister_netdevice_notifier returns -ENOENT for an absent block).
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -4212,8 +4212,13 @@
 	int i;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < MTK_MAX_DEVS; i++) {
+		struct mtk_mac *mac;
+
 		if (!eth->netdev[i])
 			continue;
+		mac = netdev_priv(eth->netdev[i]);
+		if (MTK_HAS_CAPS(eth->soc->caps, MTK_QDMA))
+			unregister_netdevice_notifier(&mac->device_notifier);
 		free_netdev(eth->netdev[i]);
 	}
 
